---
titulo: About the cave
---
This is not a portfolio. There is no résumé, no metrics, nothing for sale.

This cave is a personal archive: a place where I keep what I listen to, watch, read, study and write. It is an invitation to dive into someone's individuality —their quirks, nostalgias and contradictions— without an algorithm deciding for you what you should feel.

## A safe space from the system

Out there, almost everything we consume arrives packaged, measured and optimized. Not here. There are no ads, no trackers, no infinite feeds, no automatic recommendations. Every song, film and book is here because a person decided it mattered.

## About the music

The collections in the Curation are an act of expression: listening is a way of getting to know someone, and these songs say more about me than any biography. They are presented for expressive and educational purposes, as a curated exhibition, never as a store or as a substitute for the original works.

Every track carries its full credit and, when available, a link to the artist's official pages. If something moves you, go find it there: buy the record, go to the show, follow the people who made it. That is the best way for this cave to make sense.

{% Epigrafe autor="Jose Shōta" %}
To listen to what someone else listens to is to look through their window.
{% /Epigrafe %}
